---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · TEACHING METHODOLOGY — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero AND ITS TREATMENT IS UNTOUCHED — same
 * component, same photograph, same crop, same crumbs, same height, same title
 * and standfirst as before and as every other Academics page. All of the
 * redesign is below it.
 *
 * ⚠ THIS IS A COMBINED PAGE, AND THE COMBINATION IS THE CLIENT'S IA.
 * It carries TWO of the brief's fourteen bullets: Teaching Methodology and
 * Collaborative Learning. They belong together because collaborative learning is
 * not a separate programme at this school — it is the third of the three things
 * the school names as its method. Splitting them produced two thin pages that
 * each had to explain the other. A standalone /collaborative-learning/ route
 * existed briefly as an implementation experiment; its verified content is
 * merged here and the route is retired.
 *
 * The page was rebuilt off the generic AcStatement → AcCollage → AcSplit →
 * AcPath → AcClose system into a composed one: five sections, five compositions,
 * none of them the numeral + eyebrow + heading + paragraph + photo block the
 * client rejected as "a repeated template". Everything below the banner lives in
 * components/academics/teaching/MethodologyPage.astro, and every claim it makes
 * — and every claim it deliberately does NOT make — is sourced in that file's
 * frontmatter.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import MethodologyPage from '../../../components/academics/teaching/MethodologyPage.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/activity learning lab/DSC_1215 copy.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* ⚠ THE PANEL IS REQUIRED. PageHero is sticky and this panel covers it as the
      page scrolls; without it the banner hangs under the footer.

      ⚠ AND THE PADDING RESET IS AN INLINE STYLE, DELIBERATELY. `.u-page-panel`
      in base.css carries `padding-bottom: var(--sb-section-y)` — 120px of empty
      cream between the closing section and the footer. A stylesheet form of the
      override can be served from a different build than the HTML that needs it,
      and then it silently stops applying; an inline style travels IN the HTML,
      so the two cannot skew. Same decision as the Academic Structure pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel" style="padding-block: 0;">
    <MethodologyPage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
